One-Woman Show

1566
00:05:12,020 --> 00:05:13,960
A letter from Lord Theodore?

1567
00:05:14,310 --> 00:05:15,290
Yes.

1568
00:05:15,290 --> 00:05:19,460
I still have a dictionary he lent me, so I'm off to return it.

1569
00:05:19,460 --> 00:05:22,470
Then you will be going to the palace?

1570
00:05:22,470 --> 00:05:25,220
Yes. It's already been four days...

1571
00:05:25,220 --> 00:05:27,560
Eli, are you all right?

1572
00:05:27,560 --> 00:05:30,100
I can go return it for you.

1573
00:05:30,540 --> 00:05:35,610
Thank you. But I'll do it myself.

1574
00:05:36,850 --> 00:05:39,670
I need to make it clear where my feelings stand.

1575
00:05:42,240 --> 00:05:45,240
His Highness? I don't believe it.

1576
00:05:45,240 --> 00:05:49,710
I heard one of the prince's envoys
was seen at Earl Casull place.

1577
00:05:49,710 --> 00:05:51,750
That's Lady Irene's family, right?

1578
00:05:51,750 --> 00:05:56,750
Then is he seriously switching
from the Bernstein's fairy princess to Lady Irene instead?

1579
00:05:56,750 --> 00:05:58,740
<i>I'm a fairy princess? </i><i></i>

1580
00:05:58,740 --> 00:06:03,630
I saw His Highness and Lady Irene myself.
It looked like they were having a tryst.

1581
00:06:07,080 --> 00:06:08,580
Did we find the evidence?

1582
00:06:09,390 --> 00:06:14,980
The warehouse has been surrounded
by the third guard unit, but...

1583
00:06:14,980 --> 00:06:17,980
there's been a report that at daybreak
a number of riverboats were headed to Ulthar.

1584
00:06:19,720 --> 00:06:22,530
Is the royal guard full of idiots?

1585
00:06:22,910 --> 00:06:27,370
They were watching a warehouse on the Neville River,
but didn't keep a lookout for boats?

1586
00:06:27,370 --> 00:06:30,820
N-No! Captain Glen's deployed troops
at the river's mouth earlier

1587
00:06:30,820 --> 00:06:33,870
so we could potentially round them all up in one go.

1588
00:06:34,380 --> 00:06:39,500
It seems three days of no sleep or rest
can even make hot blooded idiots think intelligently.

1589
00:06:39,960 --> 00:06:44,170
<i>There are more guards than ever.
I should leave before I'm spotted.</i>

1590
00:06:44,170 --> 00:06:44,590
Oh ho?

1591
00:06:45,810 --> 00:06:47,970
If it isn't Lady Elianna.

1592
00:06:48,550 --> 00:06:52,220
Hello, Lord Alexei.

1593
00:06:52,220 --> 00:06:57,230
I'm glad to see you have time on your hands.
If you're headed to the archives, will you take these too?

1594
00:07:00,610 --> 00:07:01,480
Okay.

1595
00:07:01,790 --> 00:07:08,490
On the way, will you pass this along to the royal office
and ask them to resubmit the personnel affairs records?

1596
00:07:08,490 --> 00:07:09,370
And also...

1597
00:07:10,000 --> 00:07:14,000
tell him "Absurd ideas will get you nowhere."

1598
00:07:14,420 --> 00:07:16,870
O-Okay.

1599
00:07:20,270 --> 00:07:23,500
<i>I was only going to return the dictionary...</i>

1600
00:07:23,500 --> 00:07:27,120
<i>Wait, is this how it normally is?</i>

1601
00:07:32,120 --> 00:07:33,520
L-Lady Irene?!

1602
00:07:34,720 --> 00:07:35,810
Irene!

1603
00:07:36,790 --> 00:07:39,310
Irene, open your eyes!

1604
00:07:39,660 --> 00:07:41,380
How could this happen?!

1605
00:07:42,600 --> 00:07:43,980
What is this commotion?

1606
00:07:43,980 --> 00:07:46,650
It seems someone has fallen from the stairs!

1607
00:07:46,650 --> 00:07:49,640
Is she all right? Summon a doctor, quickly!

1608
00:07:51,710 --> 00:07:55,040
Oh, Irene... Are you all right?

1609
00:07:55,400 --> 00:07:56,870
What in the world happened?

1610
00:07:59,240 --> 00:08:00,500
L-Lady Elianna...

1611
00:08:00,920 --> 00:08:02,710
Lady Elianna has...!

1612
00:08:08,220 --> 00:08:10,220
What's all this uproar about?

1613
00:08:14,710 --> 00:08:16,000
Prince Chris!

1614
00:08:17,160 --> 00:08:20,850
Irene, are you hurt? Are you all right?

1615
00:08:22,780 --> 00:08:25,360
Will you tell me what happened?

1616
00:08:25,360 --> 00:08:30,150
Th-There was a misunderstanding concerning you and I.

1617
00:08:30,150 --> 00:08:35,120
I told Lady Elianna that's all it was. But...

1618
00:08:35,410 --> 00:08:41,370
Lady Elianna... blamed everything on me,

1619
00:08:41,370 --> 00:08:44,750
and I was pushed down the stairs!

1620
00:08:45,170 --> 00:08:46,760
That isn't true.

1621
00:08:47,080 --> 00:08:50,220
Has Elianna done anything else to you?

1622
00:08:50,220 --> 00:08:52,260
Y-Yes.

1623
00:08:52,260 --> 00:08:56,470
Prince Chris, I haven't been able to tell you.

1624
00:08:56,780 --> 00:08:59,180
There's no need to worry any longer.

1625
00:08:59,180 --> 00:09:02,230
In order to bring these crimes out into the open

1626
00:09:02,760 --> 00:09:06,480
will you tell us what happened in your own words?

1627
00:09:08,400 --> 00:09:16,120
Truthfully, ever since I was appointed as an apprentice
in the inner palace, I've been harassed many times.

1628
00:09:16,480 --> 00:09:22,580
I was called a low-class aristocrat,
treated as a maid, forced to skip meals...

1629
00:09:23,160 --> 00:09:26,090
and on top of that, my bed was moved to the stables...

1630
00:09:26,430 --> 00:09:32,510
All of that was done under the orders
of the future queen of the palace, Lady Elianna!

1631
00:09:33,280 --> 00:09:34,260
Huh?

1632
00:09:34,780 --> 00:09:39,720
She's become even more cruel
as I've gotten closer to Lord Glen and Lord Alexei.

1633
00:09:40,150 --> 00:09:42,520
On the day I was soaked by the drain water,

1634
00:09:42,520 --> 00:09:46,500
I was told she wanted a rose from the courtyard,
and when I went to go get one,

1635
00:09:47,270 --> 00:09:49,230
she laughed at the sight of me.

1636
00:09:49,230 --> 00:09:53,360
<i>But I didn't ask for that, nor did I laugh at her...</i>

1637
00:09:53,670 --> 00:10:00,370
I went to the archives on her request and the ladder
had been tampered with. I nearly fell off of it!

1638
00:10:00,700 --> 00:10:04,620
<i>I noticed it too, it was tampered with!</i>

1639
00:10:04,620 --> 00:10:09,630
A few days ago, 
the snacks that I got from Lady Elianna... h—

1640
00:10:09,630 --> 00:10:10,880
had bugs!

1641
00:10:13,910 --> 00:10:21,270
<i>I had no idea.
I've been an active bibliophile princess...</i>

1642
00:10:21,720 --> 00:10:24,440
You've been through quite a lot, Irene.

1643
00:10:24,440 --> 00:10:28,020
And so, unable to contain yourself,
you went straight to Elianna?

1644
00:10:28,020 --> 00:10:32,780
Yes. B-But I never dreamed she would push me...

1645
00:10:33,350 --> 00:10:37,660
And you're absolutely positive Eli pushed you, right?

1646
00:10:38,080 --> 00:10:40,790
Yes! There is no doubt in my mi—

1647
00:10:43,740 --> 00:10:46,370
She pushed you with all of that in her arms?

1648
00:10:46,370 --> 00:10:49,920
No, she couldn't have. She isn't an acrobat.

1649
00:10:52,220 --> 00:10:55,930
Uh... P-Prince Chris...

1650
00:11:06,130 --> 00:11:07,150
Good grief.

1651
00:11:08,640 --> 00:11:11,900
I'm constantly telling that Alec to quit doing that...

1652
00:11:14,240 --> 00:11:15,410
Prince Chris!

1653
00:11:15,950 --> 00:11:20,450
You must believe me! It's true, Lady Elianna—

1654
00:11:20,960 --> 00:11:23,200
Pushed you, right?

1655
00:11:23,870 --> 00:11:28,830
Y-Yes! Please, make a fair
and just decision, Your Highness!

1656
00:11:29,160 --> 00:11:34,130
Then first of all, did anyone actually witness this scene?

1657
00:11:34,130 --> 00:11:36,160
Yes, Alan saw it.

1658
00:11:36,870 --> 00:11:42,970
Yes. I witnessed Lady Irene Palcas fall down the stairs.

1659
00:11:42,970 --> 00:11:47,730
Is it true that she was pushed by Elianna?

1660
00:11:47,730 --> 00:11:50,870
Well, it would be impossible to know,
no matter who saw it.

1661
00:11:52,060 --> 00:11:57,820
Even I don't have the acrobatic ability
to push someone while playing an instrument.

1662
00:11:58,090 --> 00:12:00,110
Alan, you—!

1663
00:12:00,110 --> 00:12:04,540
In addition, if I may add from a royal court musician's ear,

1664
00:12:04,990 --> 00:12:10,540
I heard Lady Irene scream <i>before</i>
 the sound of her falling down the stairs.

1665
00:12:12,380 --> 00:12:17,050
It was as if she knew
she would be attacked before the fact.

1666
00:12:17,500 --> 00:12:19,680
What in the world are you getting at?!

1667
00:12:19,680 --> 00:12:23,050
Lastly, that was fairly ill-prepared, right, Irene?

1668
00:12:23,660 --> 00:12:26,930
You may think you've played your cards well, but...

1669
00:12:27,570 --> 00:12:30,040
you were dancing in the palm of His Highness' hand.

1670
00:12:31,090 --> 00:12:37,410
Especially today, what made the decisive blow,
was the march of father and daughter toward ruin.

1671
00:12:39,840 --> 00:12:41,130
Father?!

1672
00:12:42,390 --> 00:12:43,860
Who is that?

1673
00:12:50,330 --> 00:12:53,300
Shall we get down to business, then?

1674
00:12:56,840 --> 00:13:00,840
Irene Palcas, and your father, Viscount Palcas.

1675
00:13:01,460 --> 00:13:03,550
You are both under arrest for the assault

1676
00:13:03,550 --> 00:13:07,850
and attempted assassination of Lady Elianna Bernstein.

1677
00:13:08,930 --> 00:13:09,600
Guards!

1678
00:13:09,890 --> 00:13:12,020
<i>Assault? Assassination?!</i>

1679
00:13:12,020 --> 00:13:13,600
No, wait!

1680
00:13:15,940 --> 00:13:18,890
Your Highness! This must be some mistake!

1681
00:13:18,890 --> 00:13:20,800
<i>I'm</i> the victim here!

1682
00:13:21,940 --> 00:13:26,620
The prince who was with me is who you truly are!

1683
00:13:26,620 --> 00:13:31,090
Please! Go back to being the wise prince you were!

1684
00:13:32,820 --> 00:13:36,250
By all rights, those are words worthy of disrespect,

1685
00:13:36,540 --> 00:13:41,630
however, if false impressions have been given,
it is also my duty to correct that.

1686
00:13:42,100 --> 00:13:47,820
So, Lady Irene, let's go over your claims
 in a fair and just manner.

1687
00:13:48,930 --> 00:13:55,980
First, concerning the inner palace.
As of now, Elianna has no authority in the inner palace.

1688
00:13:55,980 --> 00:14:00,150
The one who controls that
is the current queen, my mother.

1689
00:14:00,910 --> 00:14:08,410
If your testimony is the truth, as I am the prince,
I will hold my mother accountable.

1690
00:14:08,850 --> 00:14:09,910
However,

1691
00:14:09,910 --> 00:14:14,920
on the occasion that falsehoods were spoken,
that is a crime against the royal family,

1692
00:14:14,920 --> 00:14:19,590
as well as <i>treason</i> for undermining authority.

1693
00:14:21,710 --> 00:14:24,720
Therefore, I will ask once more.

1694
00:14:24,720 --> 00:14:31,180
Lady Irene, is it true that you were
harassed in the inner palace?

1695
00:14:31,180 --> 00:14:33,320
W-Well...

1696
00:14:34,190 --> 00:14:36,440
I-I have a witness!

1697
00:14:36,440 --> 00:14:38,790
Oh, I'm sorry.

1698
00:14:38,790 --> 00:14:42,940
If you mean everything that says
you are a self-made victim, I can prove it.

1699
00:14:43,920 --> 00:14:45,280
You betrayed me.

1700
00:14:45,280 --> 00:14:49,450
Let me see, to avoid any misunderstandings
please allow me to explain something.

1701
00:14:49,450 --> 00:14:53,410
For times like this, I am His Highness' hidden trump card.

1702
00:14:53,410 --> 00:14:58,420
I keep watch to make sure there is no one
who will bring harm to Lady Elianna.

1703
00:14:58,420 --> 00:14:59,040
Huh?

1704
00:15:01,010 --> 00:15:03,300
You... you can't...

1705
00:15:03,300 --> 00:15:06,050
Lady Irene, your earlier remark...

1706
00:15:06,050 --> 00:15:09,260
Your Highness! It seems this was my mistake!

1707
00:15:09,560 --> 00:15:16,020
But I beg you to believe me!
I have never conspired to assassinate Lady Elianna!

1708
00:15:16,470 --> 00:15:19,070
You made the statement yourself.

1709
00:15:19,070 --> 00:15:21,500
The tampering of the archive ladder,

1710
00:15:21,500 --> 00:15:23,880
the contaminated snacks...

1711
00:15:24,780 --> 00:15:26,700
the water from the pipes in the rose garden...

1712
00:15:28,510 --> 00:15:32,240
The other day, when there was
that excitement from the spraying water,

1713
00:15:32,240 --> 00:15:36,830
an unidentified intruder
got into the royal palace during the fiasco.

1714
00:15:37,120 --> 00:15:40,640
Fortunately, the intruder was seized
by Glen and other royal guards, but

1715
00:15:41,750 --> 00:15:46,590
do you know anything
concerning this matter, Viscount Palcas?

1716
00:15:46,590 --> 00:15:49,840
I-I know nothing...

1717
00:15:49,840 --> 00:15:54,100
The goal of the intruder was Elianna's assassination.

1718
00:15:54,740 --> 00:15:58,230
The tampering with the ladder
and the contamination of tea leaves...

1719
00:15:58,600 --> 00:16:04,860
were both meant for Elianna, things that happened immediately
after Lady Irene began frequenting the palace.

1720
00:16:05,470 --> 00:16:09,800
The manager, my uncle Theodore, warned me about this.

1721
00:16:11,750 --> 00:16:14,740
I apologize, but can you please refrain
from coming here for the time being?

1722
00:16:15,260 --> 00:16:16,870
Lady Elianna!

1723
00:16:17,470 --> 00:16:19,370
<i>Then at that time...</i>

1724
00:16:20,420 --> 00:16:24,330
<i>they all protected me.</i>

1725
00:16:25,630 --> 00:16:27,380
This is a false accusation!

1726
00:16:28,180 --> 00:16:31,010
Someone plotted all of this!

1727
00:16:31,260 --> 00:16:32,260
To begin with,

1728
00:16:32,670 --> 00:16:38,520
is it not strange that the bibliophile princess
continues to occupy a position beyond her status?!

1729
00:16:38,880 --> 00:16:42,740
Do you truly think that person
is worthy of becoming queen?!

1730
00:16:43,480 --> 00:16:47,780
Prince Chris, you're just being deceived by her!

1731
00:16:49,440 --> 00:16:50,790
I see now...

1732
00:16:51,490 --> 00:16:56,940
I understand that your motives
differ from those of your father.

1733
00:16:59,250 --> 00:17:06,500
It's true that there is nothing I would like more than
to personally elevate my fiancée's achievements and reputation.

1734
00:17:06,820 --> 00:17:10,260
Therefore, I'll let others
speak of her accomplishments. Please begin!

1735
00:17:12,970 --> 00:17:19,390
Y-Your Highness. 
Not everything Lady Irene said is wrong.

1736
00:17:19,390 --> 00:17:20,200
Excuse me...

1737
00:17:21,240 --> 00:17:25,820
Four years ago, Lady Elianna was the one
who recognized the corruption

1738
00:17:25,820 --> 00:17:28,320
with the lords of the Weimar region.

1739
00:17:28,700 --> 00:17:34,240
Thanks to her, the seafood brought from
the Weimar fishing harbor now has the markets crowded!

1740
00:17:34,240 --> 00:17:41,710
Excuse me! The cookbooks using fish and shellfish
are so revolutionary, even we cooks are learning from it!

1741
00:17:42,000 --> 00:17:43,290
Now that I think about it,

1742
00:17:43,290 --> 00:17:47,590
books about the routines of the 
Weimar housewife are extremely popular.

1743
00:17:47,590 --> 00:17:51,260
A new variety of medicinal herbs
and their benefits have been discovered

1744
00:17:51,260 --> 00:17:54,970
from the "Oral Narratives of the East" book
that Lady Elianna sent for.

1745
00:17:55,200 --> 00:17:59,060
Last year, Lady Elianna not only predicted a massive cold front in Maldura,

1746
00:17:59,060 --> 00:18:03,440
but she also was the one who suggested
we stockpile resources to send them.

1747
00:18:03,440 --> 00:18:07,110
Thanks to her Maldora is in our debt
thanks to the provisions and aid we sent them.

1748
00:18:07,440 --> 00:18:11,690
Lady Elianna revived the Surian weave
and made it fashionable!

1749
00:18:16,910 --> 00:18:23,410
It seems everyone can also sufficiently understand
the influence and achievements of my fiancée.

1750
00:18:24,050 --> 00:18:25,290
Your Highness...

1751
00:18:28,440 --> 00:18:30,050
<i>Why does it feel like...</i>

1752
00:18:30,560 --> 00:18:35,620
<i>I'm being told "You can't escape now"?</i>

1753
00:18:37,460 --> 00:18:38,800
Your Highness.

1754
00:18:39,160 --> 00:18:41,520
I've brought Earl Casull.

1755
00:18:44,320 --> 00:18:45,090
Here.

1756
00:18:49,860 --> 00:18:56,160
One month ago, a Zelger that had been discovered
was presented by Earl Casull to the royal family.

1757
00:18:57,100 --> 00:19:00,660
An appraiser also determined it was the real deal, but...

1758
00:19:01,990 --> 00:19:04,410
This is fake, isn't it?

1759
00:19:06,640 --> 00:19:10,920
Upon a second appraisal,
it was determined to be counterfeit.

1760
00:19:11,960 --> 00:19:14,510
With this as an impetus, we took a closer look

1761
00:19:14,510 --> 00:19:19,430
and found there have been frequent incidents
of forged art pieces in the royal capital recently.

1762
00:19:19,810 --> 00:19:22,550
The mastermind was hard to track, but...

1763
00:19:23,180 --> 00:19:28,400
immediately after the suspicious death
of the appraiser who had been kept in the dark,

1764
00:19:28,400 --> 00:19:31,400
Elianna's personal life became turbulent.

1765
00:19:31,890 --> 00:19:38,490
The intention was to undermine Earl Casull
using the fake Zelger, but Elianna saw through that...

1766
00:19:38,490 --> 00:19:40,410
Perhaps this is unjustified resentment?

1767
00:19:40,760 --> 00:19:46,910
Or maybe by getting rid of her, you were hoping
to put your own daughter in her place?

1768
00:19:47,330 --> 00:19:50,720
Which is it, Viscount Palcas?

1769
00:19:51,540 --> 00:19:55,670
I-I've done neither! There is no proof of any of this!

1770
00:19:56,040 --> 00:20:01,050
Among the lumber and materials you own,
Viscount Palcas of Neville River,

1771
00:20:01,340 --> 00:20:03,510
forged materials have been discovered.

1772
00:20:03,510 --> 00:20:04,430
What?!

1773
00:20:04,820 --> 00:20:07,180
We have all the evidence we need.

1774
00:20:07,410 --> 00:20:09,270
Would you care to explain?

1775
00:20:16,110 --> 00:20:18,450
Well then, Earl Casull...

1776
00:20:18,930 --> 00:20:20,820
Regarding this counterfeiting scandal...

1777
00:20:20,820 --> 00:20:23,330
While you are also one of the victims,

1778
00:20:23,750 --> 00:20:27,080
nevertheless as the head of the family, 
you are heavily responsible.

1779
00:20:27,470 --> 00:20:31,330
I am acutely aware of the weight of my responsibility.

1780
00:20:31,840 --> 00:20:38,800
To the lady of Bernstein, who spotted the forgery
and prevented dishonor from being brought on the house,

1781
00:20:38,800 --> 00:20:41,480
I thank you wholeheartedly.

1782
00:20:42,090 --> 00:20:44,850
With your permission,

1783
00:20:45,240 --> 00:20:50,850
the Casull family would like to give our support
to Her Royal Highness, Lady Elianna Bernstein!

1784
00:20:51,250 --> 00:20:52,190
Huh?

1785
00:20:52,190 --> 00:20:53,190
He's given in.

1786
00:20:54,550 --> 00:20:58,860
The last of the nobles who would not accept Eli...

1787
00:21:00,320 --> 00:21:03,160
Thank you, Earl Casull.

1788
00:21:03,160 --> 00:21:05,830
I will gratefully accept your offering!

1789
00:21:06,390 --> 00:21:11,330
Her Royal Highness? I'm a phony...

1790
00:21:11,600 --> 00:21:15,960
I feel I should be cautious making it public like this,

1791
00:21:16,270 --> 00:21:21,470
but a moment ago, I heard everyone's
candid assessment of Elianna.

1792
00:21:21,820 --> 00:21:23,340
Therefore, let me say this!

1793
00:21:24,000 --> 00:21:32,140
Let anyone who has any objection to 
Lady Elianna Bernstein standing as my queen come forward now!

1794
00:21:43,390 --> 00:21:49,250
<i>Oh no. I thought I was supposed
to be a fiancée in name only.</i>

1795
00:21:52,870 --> 00:21:58,880
Even when you leave the stage,
I don't intend to let you go, Eli.

1796
00:22:00,030 --> 00:22:01,770
Ever since that day...

1797
00:22:03,300 --> 00:22:05,880
I've eagerly waited for this moment.

